    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="0944" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Duarte to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Portugal in the United
                            States</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By order of his excellency the minister and secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs, I have the honor to inform your excellency for such effect as may be
                    proper that on this day the Portuguese Government, in fulfillment of the award
                    of the arbitral tribunal of Berne in the matter of the litigation relative to
                    the Lourenco Marquez (Delagoa Bay) Railroad, and in order to effect a complete
                    release from its responsibility, deposits in the branch office of the Comptoir
                    d’Escompte, at London, to the joint order of the American and English
                    Governments, under the terms of the award aforesaid, the sum corresponding to
                    the awarded indemnhty, augmented by the interest, at 5 per cent, computed from
                    the 25th day of June, 1889, to the 21st of July, 1900.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity to reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. da Costa
                    Duarte.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
